libairspy 1.0.10: airspy_close() ends its libusb context (airspy_open_exit) before it frees its USB transfers (free_transfers). Each submitted
transfer holds a reference to the USB device; releasing the last one after libusb_exit() calls usbi_disconnect_device() with a null context on
libusb 1.0.27 for Windows (no hotplug support there) and crashes. This swaps the two calls. Apply with: patch -p1 < airspy-1.0.10-close-order.patch
(inside airspyone_host-1.0.10) before building the Windows airspy.dll in tools/package/cross_deps_windows.sh. OnAir keeps Airspy handles open on
Windows instead of closing them (core/src/source_airspy.cpp), which also works with the unpatched library; DECT2_AIRSPY_KEEP=0 closes them.

--- a/libairspy/src/airspy.c	2026-10-07 20:31:55
+++ b/libairspy/src/airspy.c	2026-10-07 20:31:55
@@ -1000,8 +1000,8 @@
 			pthread_cond_destroy(&device->consumer_cv);
 			pthread_mutex_destroy(&device->consumer_mp);
 
-			airspy_open_exit(device);
 			free_transfers(device);
+			airspy_open_exit(device);
 			free(device->supported_samplerates);
 			free(device);
 		}
